<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.360
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:35.700
<i>Although I was two years late for my own Coming of Age Ceremony, Miss Sochie selected me to be her partner.</i>

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.410
<i>But I never could have anticipated anything like the tradition with the leeches.</i>

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.460
<i>The White Doll reacted to Dianna Counter's WaDoms.</i>

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.930
<b>After the Ceremony</b>

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.730
There's a fire in the direction of Nocis City! Vicinity is burning too!

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.650
And you don't think the White Doll caused this fire!?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.650
That's not what happened. Can I move this?

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.660
But that big iron rod shot out fire a second ago!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.330
Was everyone at the ceremony able to get out of there okay?

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.250
They all ran off.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.250
Loran, what are you doing?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.460
I'm trying to figure out if I can drive this thing.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.050
But it doesn't have any levers or handles.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.840
What!?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.640
What is this!? We're so high up!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.220
We're like twenty or thirty meters up!

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.560
That's right.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.350
What are you doing now?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.020
Well, when I went to carve the Holy Marks on you...

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:53.940
Is it this one?

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.530
M-My Lady Sochie, are you alright?

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.450
W-What happ-

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.540
Loran, you...!

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.750
I... How did that happen?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.630
I-it can't be helped.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.340
The cockpit just suddenly dropped.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.630
What's wrong?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.550
Does the spot I bumped hurt?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.850
I guess the fish hit me...

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.680
Anyway, this machine should have some kind of operating manual.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.730
Yeah, I guess...

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.650
Loran! You have the marks carved on your back too!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.360
You mean the Holy Marks?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.530
Yeah, they're clearly carved.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.530
I can't see them.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.740
That's because this seat is uneven.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.250
<i>This seat's components are probably supposed to connect to a pilot suit.</i>

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.450
<i>That means--</i>

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.750
Miss Sochie!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.960
I'm worried about the places on fire, and I need to go find you some clothes!

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.340
<i>We keep hearing these kinds of sounds, but we can't be sure of their numbers.</i>

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.760
Hit the lights!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.850
It seems that they're only using the human type.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.640
Fire!

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.440
<i>What is that thing?</i>

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.360
Sergeant Yanni, the light we saw tearing through the sky must have been Lord Guin's new secret weapon!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:27.160
You're right. This must be our new battle strategy to defeat the Gaurians with!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.330
Listen up! The enemy's just a bunch of scarecrows!

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.750
Shoot 'em down!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.540
Fire!

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:39.840
It dodged!

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.020
Lieutenant Phil...

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.030
Have you located the source of the beam that was fired from Vicinity yet?

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.860
It doesn't appear to be a WaDom's beam.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.040
<i>It's an attack from the sky!</i>

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.750
<i>The mechanical dolls are attacking us!</i>

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.040
Kihel... Kihel, where are you?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.340
Kihel!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.630
Are you invading us!?

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:29.760
<i>The deadline we gave you passed a month ago. We told you that we wanted to return to Earth.</i>

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.560
Must you destroy our cities in order to do that?!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.730
<i>Those searchlights are interfering with my photo shooting...</i>

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:36.940
<i>You're in the way!</i>

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.940
<i>This is no time to take pictures!</i>

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.730
You won't be able to fit everyone in!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.950
<i>Can you make it up here?!</i>

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.450
l can climb!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.740
Let me on next!

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:53.950
Miss, get on board!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.460
Did Dianna Counter come here just to kill everyone?!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.330
Boss, can you make it?!

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.760
This is nothing like what they told us!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.350
They said the Terrans wouldn't put up a serious fight.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.140
Now they're flying these pain-in-the-ass toy planes, and they're even shooting at us!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.140
What's that place?

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.450
Didn't I tell you guys to just give it up already?!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.750
You can't be planning to attack us again,

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.960
not in your little toy planes!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.250
I'm serious about this!

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.050
It's a beam! It's been fired at Nocis!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.360
<i>- What kind of light is that!?
- It's just like the other one!</i>

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.740
It the same as the one that tore through the sky before!

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.450
Inform Heir Guin Rhineford about this at once!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.530
I'm afraid I can't right now.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.330
Damn it!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.750
Kihel!

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.040
Where did you go?!

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.120
I was wondering the same about you, Mother. I'm glad you didn't go out there.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.630
Now where are you going?!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.130
I need to be with Lord Guin.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.630
What should we do?

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.350
Mother!

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.350
The dummy balloons flew away!

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.730
Damn mechanical doll!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:48.230
Mother...! Mother! Open your eyes! Mother!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.440
Loran! Here.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:52.740
Thank you.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.160
Did you figure anything out?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.330
<i>Only a little.</i>

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.830
Can you move it?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.830
Of course not. But l found something that looks like the operating manual.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.620
Here, this is it.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:04.830
It's not a book?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.630
The words are stored in here.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:07.960
In there?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:08.550
Yeah.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.010
When you press here, the words appear.

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.050
Where did you find this!?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.560
Under the seat.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.850
It was stored alongside the survival kit.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.850
You've sure got the hang of this, Loran!

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.730
I can't find anything like a table of contents,

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.150
so there must be some other documents in here.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.230
<i>In that box?</i>

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.730
Why wouldn't they be?

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.030
Don't you think it's filled with lots of papers?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:35.450
I don't know. You'd better not try to open it, though.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.240
I guess not.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.450
Aren't you worried about the fires, Loran?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.660
Fires?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.430
The commander must not leave the castle!

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.060
Allow Colonel Michael to communicate with headquarters!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.150
I'm sorry. Thanks for your help.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.150
<i>No problem.</i>

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:12.530
It's hard to believe that huge mechanical doll came here from the moon.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.740
You've known about this for a long time. Isn't that just as bad?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.030
This is beyond the citizens' wildest imaginations.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:23.080
I told you, the ones attacking Nocis City are the same people we've been in contact with over the past two years.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.160
Yeah.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.040
If there's anyone I can reason with, it's Dianna Soriel.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.750
Dianna Soriel?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.050
You're great, Loran!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.340
Old timer, there's someone inside!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.260
Oh? Who could be in there?

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.630
Looks like there's two of them.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.140
Looks like you did it, Loran.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.720
That doesn't mean I'll be able to control it.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:46.060
<i>Who's up there moving the machine that came from the White Doll!?</i>

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.730
- The fire is spreading!
- Huh?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.650
<i>You're driving it, aren't you?!</i>

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.230
<i>l saw you controlling it!</i>

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.230
Are you Mr. Sid?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.150
<i>And who are you?</i>

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.530
Loran Cehack.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.150
Hey, lets go back.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.160
I heard about you from Lord Guin.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.160
This thing moved on its own earlier.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.580
We can get home pretty quickly if we use this.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:04.830
We shouldn't do that.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.160
The forbidden history...

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.500
This looks like something that was recorded in the Dark History.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.540
Is that what it is?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.540
What's the "Dark History"?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.000
Loran, try to drive it!

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.550
Can they use it?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:19.340
If you're gonna use it, then hide it in Heim Mine down in the valley!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:24.930
If this machine was recorded in the Dark History, then we can't let our enemies spot it!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.480
It moved!

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:28.940
You did it.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.940
Milady, please don't sit on my legs.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.940
Why not?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:33.940
The pedal will...

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.910
- Balancer control!
- Loran!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.490
- Get that thing under control!
- What are you doing!?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.330
Move, I'm begging you!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.930
The ground's collapsing beneath it...

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.550
Well, there's a mine entrance near here, right?

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:04.760
Did it cave in?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.910
I'm going home.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.200
Wait a minute! It's dangerous for you to go home alone!

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.830
Hey, need a hand digging this thing out?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.830
Who are you?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.410
<i>I'm the old man's assistant.</i>

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.920
<i>W-who's that?</i>

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.630
You're Master Heim's daughter, aren't you?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.500
Old man!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.210
The thing that came down is probably the driver's seat.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.010
Is that correct, Loran?

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.800
Seems that way, though I don't really know.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.430
<i>Is it all right to let them go?</i>

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.430
Just finding this one mechanical doll alone is a huge deal!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.020
I know those two well. I can ask them questions whenever I need to.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.690
Do you want me to tell Lord Guin about this?

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.530
Yes. This is one of the machines recorded in the Dark History.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:02.240
This Devilish machine started to move on it's own--

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.110
No, no, no, no. What I meant was...

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:08.540
Uh, yes. Loran Cehack was one of the kids inside it...

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.540
Yes.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:13.500
So you're saying you think other mechanical dolls may begin to appear soon.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.840
It had a gun that shoot light beams and melted?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.920
Then excavate in the region around the White Doll.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.220
You may use the Militia.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.720
Right. I'll begin at once.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.720
Oh, right, right--There's something strange about the doll they were using.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.810
What do you mean? Is it unusable?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.480
No... Well, actually, it's got a mustache!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.730
A mechanical doll with a mustache?

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.320
A mustache on the White Doll...

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.110
Sergeant Yanni, let's get out of here!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.110
Evacuate all personnel!

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.570
Take that and move it--

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.120
We can't let a bunch of scarecrows beat us!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.930
There's no way it could have been one of Dianna Counter's own.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.430
<i>That mark on the top left of where the shot was fired...</i>

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:15.440
...is where a FLAT landed two years ago.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.520
Sir.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:20.020
Could it have fallen into the hands of the militia?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.730
It was a different type of beam.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.530
Her Majesty Dianna asked us to do this peacefully, but the Earth is an immense place.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.700
Is that some kind of fighting machine?!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.700
Or is it some kind of rocket?!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.040
It can fly in the sky!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.710
We've successfully uncovered a mechanical doll that were recorded in the Dark History!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.420
Guin Rhineford...

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.000
You don't need to worry about this, Kihel Heim.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.010
If Sid's reports are correct,

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.720
then not only Inglessa, but all of Earth is home to an enormous number of space age machines!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.220
We'll obtain them and use them as weapons!

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:54.100
Weapons from a space age...?

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:58.730
Moreover, one of them was being controlled by your little sister and Laura!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.310
Doesn't that make you happy?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.530
Why do I have to carry you, Miss Sochie?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.200
Well? Why?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:17.330
I hurt my feet when I went off to look for clothes for you.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:22.630
Not to mention you're still my chauffeur, so it's your job to take me home.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.340
You have a point.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.810
Milady!

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:39.440
Sam! Miss Sochie is back!

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.360
What happened to Father?

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:47.650
My Lady...

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.700
Sam! Jessica!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.160
NO!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.830
Master Heim...!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.000
Is there anything I can do?

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:02.210
I don't know what era this comes from, but it should be a standard operating system!

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.210
Can't I get it to respond to my voice!?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.170
<i>Father!</i>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.720
It's all your fault! You were too slow!

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.310
Why didn't you save his life with the White Doll?!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:23.270
Father... Father!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.820
Milady!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.400
- Let go of me!
- Where are you going?!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.320
Nocis!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.150
I need to tell my mother and sister about this!

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:34.410
You can't! Nocis City is still under attack.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.330
You saw the fire from atop the White Doll, didn't you?!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.040
What should I do? What should I do, Loran?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.500
- I'm going!
- Don't! Please, get a hold of yourself!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.630
No!

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.710
Calm down!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:02.690
Is this...

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.020
Is <i>this</i> what Her Majesty Dianna was planning?

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.220
<i>I can't believe you were able to fire that beam cannon twice...</i>

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.680
The nanoskin is now covering the hatch, so you won't be able to open it for awhile.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.300
I can't use it?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>Ensign Poe. Lieutenant Phil would like to see you.</i>

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:39.850
Roger.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.730
Could it be... A ten-year prison sentence?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:50.320
Fifteen years. Maybe seventeen.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.110
Sir.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.030
But seeing as we're short on pilots at the moment, I can't afford to do that.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.410
So I'll give you a chance to redeem yourself.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.410
You will assist in the operation to capture that mustached mobile suit.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.710
Yes, sir! Thank you very much, sir!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:21.310
Although Madam Heim and Lady Kihel aren't here, we're left with no other choice but to do this now, Lady Sochie.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.730
Although you seem to have a become a bit feverish,

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.730
we still need you to sign this document.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:27.980
Go ahead, Little miss.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.200
<i>Keith, you idiot! What are you doing here?!</i>

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.820
<i>Come on now, My Lady.</i>

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.200
Place the dirt onto the Master's coffin.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:54.130
Let it all out. You can cry all you want now.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.300
Hey, hurry up!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.010
<i>Is the gravestone ready?</i>

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.720
No. All we have is this.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:07.520
As long as they don't mix up the names, this'll be fine.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.440
Why'd you have to come here now?

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.400
Looks like Vicinity's in bad shape too.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:15.030
Well, then. If I see the mustache, I'll hold my ground

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.240
let the WaDs surround him, and capture him.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:19.530
Don't fall behind!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.340
The controls look a bit complicated, but it seems to be pretty well built.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.340
Do you really think it's from an era two or three thousand years ago?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:39.300
Maybe the Moonrace buried it here a hundred or so years ago.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.800
You think so?

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.140
Oh, I saw four large beams fired off last night.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.810
Did you do that?

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.810
I didn't fire more than once.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.230
At the WaDom?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.810
I wasn't controlling it.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.310
l haven't even figured out how to read the manual yet.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:57.030
Yeah. Your attack probably shocked them so much that they fought back.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.320
- You're probably right about that.
 -Yeah.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.320
So what do you think is gonna happen now?

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.410
Don't waste your time thinking about it.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.620
There's no way they'll go to war.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.330
But the militia fought back, right?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.910
You idiot, you call that "fighting back"?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.370
Last night, the WaDoms caused a ton of damage.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.500
I myself fled because I wanted to save the baker's daughter.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.300
We should probably dig up the FLAT and go meet with Dianna Counter.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.220
I know, but I don't want to go back.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:21.800
Why not?

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:25.220
Because the two year observation period is over.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:29.770
We can go anywhere on Earth we want now. Our job ended yesterday.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:34.110
You have a point. I'm gonna go somewhere without the war and reopen the bakery.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.110
Go somewhere without war and make bread?

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:41.030
Or should I bring the FLAT to the ship in exchange for their protection?

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.410
What are you saying?!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.820
Is your own safety the only thing you care about, Keith?

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.120
Don't you care about the people of the Earth at all?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.330
That's not what I meant.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:53.330
Once you see how powerful their mobile suits are, you'll want to run away too.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.000
You think I'd run away?

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.510
If you saw the damage in Nocis, you would!

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.630
I'd never think about doing something like that!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:03.010
But almost anything can happen in a war!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:07.310
You really don't have any imagination, do you?

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.310
So it is a war?

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.520
Yes, it is.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.810
Her Majesty Dianna...

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.520
Keith!

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.520
We had specific orders not to bring any personal belongings with us.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.530
Knock it off.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:20.110
You're pretty sneaky.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.400
You brought Queen Dianna's...

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.610
It's a copy. Just a copy.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.330
Do you think Her Majesty Dianna can get all this settled when she arrives?

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.040
Would Dianna Soriel bother coming to the Earth in person?

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.710
But she wants all of the Moonrace to come back to Earth!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.420
<i>Here.</i>

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.500
What are you doing?

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.630
<i>I'm worried about my boss in Nocis.</i>

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:40.960
Makes sense.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:46.140
Loran, you'll have to learn how to use that mustached mobile suit.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:47.970
Why?

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.220
In order to meet up with Dianna Counter,

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.850
or to escape.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:00.820
Dana! Here comes the Heim Family's driver.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.320
Is that him?

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.740
Be careful on the road.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:09.030
Is this really a telegram sent by Lord Guin Sard Rhineford?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.910
Give me a hand here.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.120
R-right!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:13.120
<i>I'm giving you that telegram, Laura.</i>

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.210
Sir!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.830
It's a letter of appointment.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.330
What's that?

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.000
It means you're gonna officially be driving this thing as a militia member.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.090
No way!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.010
We've made contact with an unknown enemy,

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.800
so we need battle strength.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:25.720
Battle strength?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.680
Do you use these things on the right and left sides of the seat to control it?

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.010
Yeah, that's what it said in the manual.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:34.810
I don't completely understand the technology of the Dark History,

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.730
but it's something like this.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:38.940
<i>Hey, Joseph!</i>

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.730
The display turned on.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.610
Mr. Joseph, it's alright.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.400
The radar is... detecting mobile suits?

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.160
I can do it!

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.120
I think I can get it to stand.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.330
Please stand back!

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.120
Give it a shot!

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.710
It looks like the enemy is approaching us.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.420
I'll go investigate!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.560
<i>Whether it be the militia or Dianna Counter,</i>

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.400
<i>it doesn't really matter which side starts things.</i>

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:48.690
<i>War can make peoples' hearts turn ugly,</i>

00:23:48.690 --> 00:23:51.780
<i>which causes people to lose their lives.</i>

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:56.990
<i>But I never truly realized this.</i>

00:23:58.490 --> 00:24:01.080
<i>Next time, on Turn-A Gundam,</i>

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.290
<i>Soldiers From the Homeland</i>

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.290
<i>"Though it's summer, the wind is chilly."</i>

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:08.380
<b>Soldiers From the Homeland</b>
